+# Captain Notes
+
+## Durable decisions
+
+- **Root cause of acceptance test failure**: In a real browser, clicking a checkbox natively toggles `.checked` AND our `click` handler fires on the same event. These two DOM mutations cause Cypress to detect a "page update" when commands are chained (e.g. `.click().should('be.checked')`), because the subject appears to be detached between the browser's native mutation and our handler's mutation.
+- **Fix**: Intercept `mousedown` on `.toggle` checkboxes with `preventDefault()` so the browser never natively toggles `checked`. Our `toggleTodo` handler alone manages `checked` via the data model, producing a single deterministic DOM mutation per click.
+
+## Specs changed
+
+- None (production defect fix only)
+
+## Production code changed
+
+- `js/app.js` – added `mousedown` handler with `preventDefault()` on `.toggle` checkboxes; restored explicit `cb.checked = updated.completed` in `toggleTodo`
+
+## Verification
+
+- cucumber-js (happy-dom): 24/24 scenarios, 158/158 steps passed before and after fix
+
